.TH SKIPPY-WL 1 "" "skippy-wl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skippy-wl \- window overview for labwc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skippy-wl \-\-daemon
.br
.B skippy-wl
.RB { \-\-toggle | \-\-show }
.RB [ \-\-app\-id
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-title
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-status
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-next | \-\-prev ]
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-show \-\-multi\-select
.RB [ \-\-app\-id
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-title
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-status
.IR LIST ]
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-switch
.RB [ \-\-app\-id
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-title
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-status
.IR LIST ]
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-activate
.I identifier
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-quit
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a fullscreen overlay with a thumbnail of every window on every output.
Windows are ordered most recently used first (as seen by the running daemon). Pick one to focus it. Windows on other workspaces and minimized windows are listed too.
.PP
Run one daemon, then bind
.B skippy-wl \-\-toggle
to a key in the compositor. Without a daemon,
.B \-\-show
and
.B \-\-toggle
show the overlay once in their own process.
.PP
Needs these Wayland protocols: ext-foreign-toplevel-list, ext-image-capture-source,
ext-image-copy-capture, wlr-foreign-toplevel-management and wlr-layer-shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Track windows and listen on the control socket until
.BR \-\-quit ,
SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Open the overlay, or close it if it is open.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Open the overlay. Does nothing if it is open.
.TP
.B \-\-show \-\-multi\-select
Pick several windows. A click or
.B Space
toggles the window, a toggled window is tinted. The focused window starts selected. Nothing is focused. On
.B Enter
the identifiers of the toggled windows are printed to stdout, one per line, in the order they were toggled. On cancel, or with nothing toggled, nothing is printed and the exit status is 1. Close and minimize are disabled. Runs in its own process, not in the daemon.
.TP
.BI \-\-activate " identifier"
Focus the window with that toplevel identifier, such as one printed by
.BR "\-\-show \-\-multi\-select" .
Unminimizes the window and switches to its workspace. Exits 1 if no such window exists or it cannot be activated. Runs in its own process.
.TP
.B \-\-switch
Focus the previous window at once and draw nothing: the second window in the usage order, or the first if no window has focus.
.br
Takes the filters below, so
.I \-\-switch \-\-app\-id kitty
flips between the last two kitty windows.
.br
Needs the daemon. Does nothing if the overlay is open. Ignores
.B switch.pivot
and
.BR switch.wait .
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH SWITCH MODE
.TP
.B \-\-next
Open on the previous window (second in the order). Hold the modifier of the key binding, press
.B Tab
to step forward, or run
.B \-\-next
again. Run
.B \-\-prev
to step back. Release the modifier to focus the selected window, unless you paused for longer than
.BR switch.hold .
.TP
.B \-\-prev
Open on the last window. Run it again to step back.
.PP
If the modifier is released before
.B switch.wait
passes, the window is focused without drawing the overlay. With no modifier held, the switch happens at once.
.SH FILTERS
.BR \-\-show ,
.B \-\-toggle
and
.B \-\-switch
take filters that limit which windows are listed. All given filters must match.
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-id " LIST"
Match the window's app id (the class), for example
.IR kitty,foot .
.TP
.BI \-\-title " LIST"
Match the window title, for example
.IR "*vim*" .
.TP
.BI \-\-status " LIST"
Match the window state:
.BR minimized ,
.BR maximized ,
.BR fullscreen
or
.BR activated .
.PP
A
.I LIST
is comma separated glob patterns (* ? [...]), case insensitive; spaces around terms are ignored and \\, is a literal comma. A window matches if it matches any plain term and none of the terms that start with
.BR ! .
Examples:
.IR "\-\-app\-id 'kitty,foot'" ,
.IR "\-\-app\-id '!firefox'" ,
.IR "\-\-status minimized" ,
.IR "\-\-app\-id kitty \-\-status '!minimized'" .
.PP
A window whose state is not known (the compositor gave no matching handle) never matches a
.B \-\-status
filter. Nothing is shown if no window matches. Quote patterns so the shell does not expand them.
.SH OVERLAY KEYS
Defaults. Change them with
.B [bind]
in the config file.
.TP
.B Left Right Up Down
Move the selection.
.TP
.B Home End
First or last window.
.TP
.B Tab, Shift+Tab
Next or previous window.
.TP
.B Return
Focus the selected window (with \-\-multi\-select: confirm).
.TP
.B Delete
Close the selected window.
.TP
.B m
Minimize the selected window, or restore it if it is minimized.
.TP
.B / or any unbound key
Type to filter: only windows whose app id or title contains the text stay. While the filter is open every printable key types, including bound letters such as m. Backspace deletes a character (on an empty filter it closes the filter).
.TP
.B Escape
Clear the filter. With no filter: close the overlay (with \-\-multi\-select: cancel).
.PP
Mouse: hover selects, left click focuses (toggles with \-\-multi\-select), middle click closes the window, left click on empty space closes the overlay.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.config/skippy-wl/skippy-wl.rc
(or
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/skippy-wl/skippy-wl.rc ).
One
.I key = value
per line, grouped under
.I [section]
headers. A line that starts with
.B #
is a comment, and so is the rest of a line after a
.B #
that follows whitespace. Lines may be up to 255 characters. A key outside a section is an error. The settings below are named
.IR section.key . The file is read each time the overlay opens. Invalid lines are reported on stderr and skipped.
.TP
.B layout.margin
Pixels between the screen edge and the grid. Default 48.
.TP
.B layout.spacing
Pixels between tiles. Default 28.
.TP
.B tiles.radius
Corner radius in pixels, 0 to 50, of each window preview, its border and the selection frame. 0 keeps them square. Default 0.
.TP
.B label.show
Show a label on each tile. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B label.option
.BR windowTitle ,
.B windowClass
(the app id) or
.BR both .
Default
.IR windowTitle .
.TP
.B label.position
.B below
puts the label under the tile and reserves room for it. The others put it inside the tile:
.BR top\-left ,
.BR top ,
.BR top\-right ,
.BR left ,
.BR center ,
.BR right ,
.BR bottom\-left ,
.B bottom
and
.BR bottom\-right .
Default
.IR below .
.TP
.B label.offsetX
.TQ
.B label.offsetY
Pixels to move the label from its position, \-4000 to 4000. It may leave the tile; labels are drawn above all previews, the selected one on top. Default 0.
.TP
.B label.height
Box height in pixels, 8 to 200; with
.B below
the room reserved under the tile is 4 pixels more, the gap between the tile frame and the box. The inside positions keep the same gap from the frame. Default 28.
.TP
.B label.width
Box width as a fraction of the tile width, 0.1 to 1. Default 0.92.
.TP
.B label.radius
Corner radius of the box in pixels, 0 to 50; at most half the box height. Default 6.
.TP
.B label.border
.TQ
.B label.background
.TQ
.B label.backgroundHighlight
Box colors as #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA. The highlight is for the selected tile and defaults to
.BR label.background .
Default fully transparent.
.TP
.B label.opacity
0 to 255, scales the border and background alpha. Default 255.
.TP
.B label.text
.TQ
.B label.textOutline
Text and outline colors. Default #ffffff and no outline.
.TP
.B label.font
Pango font description, or skippy\-xd style such as
.IR IosevkaTermNF:size=12:weight=bold .
Also sets the font of the filter bar. Default
.IR "Sans 11" .
.TP
.B monitors.mode
.B each
shows the windows of each monitor on that monitor.
.B pointer
shows all windows on the monitor the pointer enters when the overlay opens; the other monitors stay empty.
Default
.IR each .
.TP
.B switch.pivot
switch mode: focus the selected window when the modifiers held at open are released.
.B false
leaves the overlay open until Enter, a click or Escape. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B switch.wait
Milliseconds to wait before drawing the overlay in switch mode (needs
.BR switch.pivot ).
0 draws at once. Default 100.
.TP
.B switch.hold
Milliseconds. In switch mode, releasing the modifiers more than this long after the overlay was drawn or the last key press leaves the overlay open for the mouse and keys. Running the command again makes the next release pick. 0 always picks on release. Needs
.BR switch.pivot .
Default 1000.
.TP
.B icons.enabled
.B true
draws the application icon on each tile, and large in the middle of tiles without a thumbnail. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B icons.size
Size in pixels, 16 to 256, of the icon. Default 48. Use 28 to 64: tiles smaller than three times this have no icon, so larger values hide icons when many windows are open. Tiles without a thumbnail show a larger icon sized to the tile.
.TP
.B icons.position
Where the icon sits on the tile:
.BR top\-left ,
.BR top ,
.BR top\-right ,
.BR left ,
.BR center ,
.BR right ,
.BR bottom\-left ,
.B bottom
or
.BR bottom\-right .
Default
.IR bottom\-right .
An icon and a
.B label.position
inside the tile at the same place overlap.
.TP
.B icons.theme
Icon theme name. Its parents and
.B hicolor
are searched too. Default
.IR hicolor .
.TP
.B animation.enabled
.B true
fades the overlay in and grows the tiles slightly when it opens. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B animation.duration
Milliseconds the open animation takes, 0 to 1000. 0 shows the overlay at once. Default 150.
.TP
.B background.image
PNG, JPEG, AVIF, HEIC or HEIF file drawn behind the tiles, scaled to fill each monitor. A leading
.B ~/
is expanded. Default none.
.TP
.B background.image_cmd
Shell command that prints the image path on its first line. It runs each time the overlay opens, so the image follows wallpaper changes. A command that exits non-zero, prints nothing or takes longer than a second is ignored and
.B background.image
is used instead. A
.B #
after a space starts a comment, so keep it out of the command. Example:
.IR "noctalia msg wallpaper-get" .
Default none.
.TP
.B background.panels
.B show
keeps panels and docks visible: the overlay fills only the space they leave free, so
.B background.image
is scaled to that smaller area. It works for panels that reserve space and the panels stay clickable; the compositor decides how layers are arranged.
.B hide
covers them. Default
.IR hide .
.TP
.B colors.background
Overlay color as #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA. Default #000000ff. With an alpha below ff the desktop shows through; with
.B background.image
it tints the image when set, and is not drawn when unset. Use #00000000 for a fully transparent overlay.
.TP
.B colors.highlight
Selection color as #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA. Default #5999ff.
.TP
.B colors.border
Border of unselected tiles, #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA. Default #ffffff2e.
.TP
.B colors.theme_file
Labwc theme file, read each time the overlay opens. Only a leading
.B ~/
is expanded. The selected tile uses
.B window.active.border.color
and other tiles use
.B window.inactive.border.color
at 60% alpha.
.B colors.highlight
and
.B colors.border
in the config file win. Example:
.IR ~/.local/share/themes/noctalia/openbox-3/themerc .
.TP
.B hide.app_id hide.title hide.status
Comma separated globs, same syntax as
.B \-\-app\-id
and
.BR \-\-title .
A window that matches any of them is never shown, also not by
.BR \-\-switch .
A leading
.B !
hides every window except the matches. hide.status takes the names of
.BR \-\-status .
A window whose state is not known is not hidden by it. Empty by default.
.TP
.B bind.select bind.cancel bind.close bind.minimize bind.left bind.right bind.up bind.down bind.home bind.end bind.next bind.prev
Keys of the [bind] section, for example
.IR "select = Return" .
Up to four xkb keysym names, comma separated. A line replaces the default keys of that action. A key moves from its old action to the new one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/skippy-wl.sock
Control socket of the daemon.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/skippy-wl/skippy-wl.rc
Config template.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/systemd/user/skippy-wl.service
User service for the daemon.
.SH LABWC
In
.IR ~/.config/labwc/autostart :
.PP
.nf
skippy-wl \-\-daemon &
.fi
.PP
In
.IR ~/.config/labwc/rc.xml :
.PP
.nf
<keybind key="A\-Tab">
  <action name="Execute" command="skippy\-wl \-\-toggle"/>
</keybind>
.fi
.SH SYSTEMD
Remove the autostart line, then add to
.IR ~/.config/labwc/autostart ,
in this order:
.PP
.nf
systemctl \-\-user import\-environment WAYLAND_DISPLAY
systemctl \-\-user start skippy\-wl.service
.fi
.PP
Do not run
.B systemctl \-\-user enable
on it.
.PP
Stop a running daemon first:
.BR "skippy\-wl \-\-quit" .
.PP
After an upgrade:
.BR "systemctl \-\-user daemon\-reload" ,
then
.BR "systemctl \-\-user restart skippy\-wl.service" .
.PP
Before
.BR "install.sh \-\-uninstall" :
.BR "systemctl \-\-user stop skippy\-wl.service" .
.PP
Logs:
.BR "journalctl \-\-user \-u skippy\-wl" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error, 3 if \fB\-\-daemon\fR finds another daemon running.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR labwc (1)
